  "reason": "With zero completed experiments, there is no evidence to guide exploitation, so the priority is establishing a clean, interpretable baseline. config_001 (RNA-only, singleprofile, PCA n2000) is the simplest configuration in the design space: a single modality, the simplest profile setting, and a standard linear encoder with no learned parameters. This gives a well-defined reference performance against which all subsequent experiments (multiprofile aggregation, alternative RNA encoders, image-only, and multimodal fusion) can be meaningfully compared. If multimodal or multiprofile models later fail to exceed this simple baseline, that is a critical finding about where added complexity is unhelpful. Starting here minimizes confounding (no aggregation, no fusion, no image) and reduces uncertainty about whether the basic RNA signal is informative at all, making it the most efficient first use of the experiment budget."
